WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.963 --> 00:00:12.444
One afternoon Mrs.

2
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:14.066
Hamilton was making dinner.

3
00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:19.090
Suddenly an uninvited guest scurried into her kitchen.

4
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.892
"Eek! There's a mouse!

5
00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:23.373
There's a mouse!"

6
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:24.614
screamed Mrs.

7
00:00:24.654 --> 00:00:30.058
Hamilton. you all right, dear?"

8
00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:31.159
asked Mr.

9
00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:34.365
Hamilton. "No, I am not all right.

10
00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:37.027
There is a mouse in my house!"

11
00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:39.289
Mrs. Hamilton said angrily.

12
00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:41.590
"What should we do?"

13
00:00:42.091 --> 00:00:42.831
asked Jason.

14
00:00:42.851 --> 00:00:44.492
"I've got it!"

15
00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:46.534
Mr. Hamilton said suddenly.

16
00:00:46.554 --> 00:00:48.415
"We'll get a cat!"

17
00:00:52.998 --> 00:00:54.579
The next day Mr.

18
00:00:54.619 --> 00:00:56.460
Hamilton went to buy a cat.

19
00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.142
"Did you get the cat?"

20
00:00:59.542 --> 00:01:00.863
asked Jason when Mr.

21
00:01:00.923 --> 00:01:01.984
Hamilton got home.

22
00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:05.089
A little head appeared from Mr.

23
00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.069
Hamilton's arms.

24
00:01:06.089 --> 00:01:09.771
"Meow," it said in a tiny voice.

25
00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:12.512
"Hello, cat!"

26
00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:13.633
said Jason.

27
00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:18.375
"You need a name since you will be part of the family."

28
00:01:19.395 --> 00:01:20.496
Jason and Mr.

29
00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:23.857
Hamilton tried to think of a name for a long time.

30
00:01:24.778 --> 00:01:25.758
Finally Mr.

31
00:01:25.798 --> 00:01:28.059
Hamilton said, "I know.

32
00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:33.466
We will call you Snatch, since you will snatch up the mice in our house."

33
00:01:37.188 --> 00:01:41.610
Later that day Jason began to train the cat to catch mice.

34
00:01:42.451 --> 00:01:44.812
He showed Snatch a little toy mouse.

35
00:01:44.832 --> 00:01:47.774
"This is a mouse," he said.

36
00:01:47.794 --> 00:01:51.256
"When you see a mouse, pounce on it."

37
00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:55.118
Snatch was a very active cat.

38
00:01:55.878 --> 00:01:58.380
She loved to chase butterflies and birds.

39
00:01:59.576 --> 00:02:01.158
"Look how fast she is!"

40
00:02:01.658 --> 00:02:03.460
Mr. Hamilton said proudly.

41
00:02:04.761 --> 00:02:07.563
Mrs. Hamilton held a treat in her hand.

42
00:02:08.344 --> 00:02:10.486
Then Snatch jumped up to eat it.

43
00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.489
"Look how high she can jump!"

44
00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:15.911
Mrs. Hamilton said proudly.

45
00:02:17.132 --> 00:02:18.753
Snatch learned quickly.

46
00:02:19.654 --> 00:02:23.317
Jason liked to test her when she didn't know he was there.

47
00:02:23.337 --> 00:02:26.060
"Snatch! It's a mouse!"

48
00:02:26.748 --> 00:02:30.030
Jason threw the toy mouse for Snatch to catch.

49
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:33.553
"Look how smart she is!"

50
00:02:33.913 --> 00:02:35.254
cried Jason proudly.

51
00:02:35.274 --> 00:02:40.838
"She is so fast," said Mr.

52
00:02:40.878 --> 00:02:45.641
Hamilton. "She is so strong," said Mrs.

53
00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:50.084
Hamilton. "She is so smart," said Jason.

54
00:02:52.848 --> 00:02:56.551
Mrs. Hamilton went to the kitchen to get some ice cream.

55
00:02:56.571 --> 00:02:59.334
"Yeek! It's a mouse!

56
00:02:59.694 --> 00:03:00.855
It's a mouse!"

57
00:03:01.295 --> 00:03:02.096
she screamed.

58
00:03:03.397 --> 00:03:05.259
Everyone ran into the kitchen.

59
00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:07.000
"Go, Snatch!

60
00:03:07.441 --> 00:03:08.502
Get the mouse!"

61
00:03:08.842 --> 00:03:09.522
they cried.

62
00:03:11.864 --> 00:03:14.527
Snatch chased the mouse into a corner.

63
00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:16.708
The mouse was trapped!

64
00:03:16.728 --> 00:03:19.070
"Good work, Snatch!"

65
00:03:19.511 --> 00:03:20.552
shouted the family.

66
00:03:21.596 --> 00:03:23.698
Snatch got closer to the mouse.

67
00:03:30.804 --> 00:03:34.347
Suddenly the little mouse bit Snatch on the nose.

68
00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:37.990
Snatch meowed and ran out of the room.

69
00:03:39.171 --> 00:03:41.272
The Hamiltons were disappointed.

70
00:03:43.894 --> 00:03:46.136
The Hamiltons held a family meeting.

71
00:03:46.156 --> 00:03:48.558
"What do we do now?"

72
00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:49.859
asked Mrs.

73
00:03:49.919 --> 00:03:56.916
Hamilton. Everyone wanted to get rid of the mouse, but now Snatch was afraid of mice.

74
00:03:58.357 --> 00:04:00.279
So the next day, Mr.

75
00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:02.580
Hamilton put out a mousetrap.

76
00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:07.324
"I thought all cats caught mice," said Jason.

77
00:04:07.344 --> 00:04:11.046
"I guess not," said Mr.

78
00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:18.572
Hamilton. Snatch was not good at catching real mice, but everyone loved her anyway.
